<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Coele-Syria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Coele-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, meaning &quot;hollow Syria&quot;, was the name used in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a> for the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicia">Phoenicia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>. It was disputed between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> in a series of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syrian-wars">Syrian Wars</a>. The Seleucids won it permanently after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-panium">Battle of Panium</a> around 200 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/coele-syria.jpg" alt="Coele-Syria" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Robert Shepherd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Asia_minor-Shepherd_1923_Syria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The principal conflicts were the Syrian Wars against the Seleucid Empire, fought over control of <b>Coele-Syria</b> and other strategic territories.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ptolemaic-empire">Ptolemaic Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…Antiochus led the cavalry and elephants to rout the Ptolemaic army under the Aetolian general Scopas, permanently secured <b>Coele-Syria</b>; but the invasion of Greece in 192 BCE and the ensuing war with Rome ended in catastrophic defeat at the Battle of Magnesia in 190 BCE, where a Roman…</blockquote><a href="/empire/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The battle determined the sovereignty of <b>Coele-Syria</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-22">22 June in history</a></li></ul></section>
